+    replaying it starts them all at once. It is the same kernels on the same
+    memory every time, so the inputs of a call are copied to where the
+    recorded call had its inputs, and the results are copies of what the
+    recorded call left where it had its results: every call gets tensors of
+    its own, as it does from the code itself. A caller that hands over the
+    same memory again and again (one buffer it fills, a few it goes round)
+    gets a recording that reads the inputs where they are, and no copy; and
+    such a recording is started as soon as the region is called, before the
+    call is looked at (``ahead``): the GPU works while the CPU checks.
+
